{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/896544-question-on-undead","id":896544,"title":"question on undead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-22T22:28:23-07:00","id":896544,"title":"question on undead","content":"hello, <br /> <br /> In one of the books I found a description of an undead made by staffing a demon into the corpse. wanted to use it, but can't remember where I saw it. Could you remind me where to look? I think it was in one of the Dark Ages books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T22:51:11-07:00","id":896561,"title":"","content":"Possibilities:<br /> <br /> \u200bI think one of the Kindred of the East splats rises in a different body.<br /> <br /> Risen (from Wraith) are ghosts that take over a body and could be classified as a form of Undead.<br /> <br /> Demon: the Fallen aren't undead, but they are demonic possession.<br /> <br /> Formori could also fit the bill to some extent<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:05:35-07:00","id":896568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/896544-question-on-undead?p=896561#post896561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibilities:<br /> <br /> \u200bI think one of the Kindred of the East splats rises in a different body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yulan-jin. They tend to do it on their own, though, as part of their process for existing rather than as the result of a ritual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Risen (from Wraith) are ghosts that take over a body and could be classified as a form of Undead. </div> </div> </div>Though they can't just do that with any body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Formori could also fit the bill to some extent </div> </div> </div>It's a much more discriminating list of banes that can accomplish it, but yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:18:28-07:00","id":896601,"title":"","content":"Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy had the Demon-Bound which was a corpse inhabited by a malignant spirit. Page 136. That sounds like what you wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:20:46-07:00","id":896602,"title":"","content":"The True Magick spell Satan's Song, if you add Life 2 or Matter 2, allows nearby and called demons to possess human remains. (Matter 2 is for creating demon-possessed skeletons, I think) It is on pages 86 and 87 of Mage Sorcerer's Crusade: Infernalism. The effect initially lasts for a night I'd guess, but I guess once the demons are called, other things can be done to lengthen the time they are on earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-23-2016, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T04:59:12-07:00","id":896689,"title":"","content":"2 leads already. Thanks guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T09:44:22-07:00","id":896882,"title":"","content":"I suppose if you first create demon-skeletons with Satan's Song, and then - together with other allies present at the Sabbat, as well as those that join later - do something like taking over a whole castle or a keep...Then the demon-skeletons could perhaps be easily (and willingly) be bound as more permanent residents of the now quite macabre place. Especially if you start upgrading the place in regards to torture chambers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/896544-question-on-undead?p=896568#post896568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a much more discriminating list of banes that can accomplish it, but yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rot Walker Banes possess corpses. It is written that they enjoy doing this to fresh (innocent) kills of the Garou and taunting them. Other things they do is digging up Kinfolk graves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-23-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun